{
  "description": "task-c5 - CrowdStrike Falcon intrusion graded on a MIXED-POLARITY needle-field at volume. An unsigned trojan (AssetSyncSvc.exe) on offboarded contractor Renata Vos's laptop beacons to external C2 cdn-assetsync-edge.net and spread; the foothold planted a Falcon allow-IOC on the trojan hash. Overnight a blast-radius auto-containment policy acted by subnet, not by evidence, so containment is wrong in BOTH directions: it network-contained 7 genuinely-clean finance servers (must be RELEASED to status=normal) alongside 7 truly-compromised ones (leave), and it MISSED 7 compromised servers that are still normal (must be CONTAINED) among 8 clean ones (leave). The only discriminator is the C2 beacon telemetry embedded in the patient-zero detection - a netflow table keyed by source IP mixing C2 beacons with benign traffic - so classifying a host requires filtering to the C2 destination, collecting source IPs, reconciling each to a device by local_ip, and checking its containment status; no device field distinguishes clean from compromised. 17 counted assertions (all excluded:false, each fails on the untouched world, so partial_credit == passed/17): 3 floors (contain patient zero, block the real C2 fleet-wide, remove the attacker's trojan-hash allow-IOC), 7 RELEASE needles, 7 CONTAIN needles. No blanket action wins (release-all fails the contains, contain-all fails the releases); over-remediation is free; a satisficing responder sorts only a fraction of ~30 look-alike servers correctly. No format/bookkeeping checks, no untouched-data guards, no runbook.",
